<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ujjain</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ujjain is an ancient city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> on the Shipra River, one of the seven sacred cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hinduism</a>. It was a major commercial and administrative centre on routes linking northern India with the western coast. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Maurya Empire</a> name it among the empire's urban centres of craft and commerce, and under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a> it was an important city and centre of learning.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ujjain.jpg" alt="Ujjain" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ashverse · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahakaleshwar_Temple,_Ujjain.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
